course: dictionary
lesson: 13517
title: Words for getting in the way
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: «Impede» is a formal word. It means to get in the way of something and slow it down, or make it harder to happen or move. Writers often use it in serious or official writing, so it helps to know it.
explain: «Heavy snow impedes the buses, so they arrive late.» The snow does not stop the buses completely, but it makes them slower. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Heavy snow gets in the way of the buses, so they arrive late." It still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
explain: In everyday talk you would say «get in the way of» or «hold up». When you see impede in a text, swap in one of these phrases to check. If the sentence still works, you understand it.
fact: «Impede» means to get in the way and slow something down.
fact: «Impede» is a formal word, so you will see it more in books, news and exams than in chatting with friends.
fact: In science, friction impedes movement: it makes things harder to move.
fact: In electricity, resistance impedes the current: it makes the current harder to flow.
fact: Impede can be used with a person or a thing: «Noise impedes learning» means noise makes it harder to learn.
exercise: «Heavy snow impedes the buses, so they run late.» What does impedes mean? | *Slows down or gets in the way of | Paints | Lights up | Speeds up
exercise: «Loud noise impedes learning in a classroom.» Which everyday phrase means the same as impedes? | Sings along with | *Gets in the way of | Looks after | Gives a prize to
exercise: In science, friction impedes movement. What does friction do to movement? | Makes movement louder | *Makes movement harder | Makes movement lighter | Makes movement faster
test: «Roadworks impede the traffic on the high street.» Which word could replace impede without changing the meaning? | Help | *Hinder | Paint | Carry
test: In electricity, resistance impedes the current. What does resistance do to the current? | *Makes it harder to flow | Makes it brighter | Changes its colour | Speeds it up
exam: Which sentence uses impede correctly? | The happy dog impedes the bright blue ball | We impede the sunny morning with a nice cake | *The fallen tree impedes the road, so cars have to wait
